<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 7.16 pct, M2 up 3.67 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 7.16 pct, M2 up 3.67 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 1.429 trillion levs on August 8 from 1.334 trillion levs a week earlier and M2 increased to 4.767 trillion levs from 4.598 trillion, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 3.51 percent to 4.993 trillion levs in the week to August 8.</p>
<p>Conversion of foreign currency-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixing of 1,000 levs per mark for August 8, August 1 and July 25.</p>
<p>The lev was pegged at 1,000 per mark on July 1 under a currency board system, a form of an IMF-prescribed fixed exchange rate mechanism aimed at restoring confidence in the lev and stabilising the economy.</p>
<p>The system requires levs in circulation and banks' accounts at the central bank to be fully matched by central bank's Issue Department assets, which make up central bank foreign exchange reserves.</p>
